Environmental protection research and development include:
- Identification and analysis of sources of pollution, dispersion of pollutants in the environment, effects of pollution on human beings, species and the biosphere;
- R&D for the prevention and elimination of all forms of pollution; 
- R&D oriented towards equipment and instruments of pollution measurement and analysis.

Management of water include:
- Water restoration, measuring and monitoring equipment;
- Closed-circuit cooling systems;
- Sea water de-salination plants;
- Rainwater storage tanks;
- Detecting and fixing leaks.

Note: Water supply charges are not included.

