Wastewater management include:
- Equipment in wastewater treatment plants; 
- Equipment for cleaning discharges or detecting leaks; 
- Equipment for the measurement of discharges or pollutant concentrations; 
- Equipment for the storage and transport of wastewater, e.g. septic tanks, mains sewage network connections; 
- Labour costs of operating and maintaining wastewater treatment plants; 
- Wastewater collection services provided by external companies.

Minimisation of the intake of fossil resources for non-energy purposes include:
- Plastic recycling equipment;
- Recycled plastic materials.

Noise and vibration abatement include:
- Constructions to dampen vibrations and absorb noise; 
- Screens and other barriers to reduce noise; 
- Soundproof windows; 
- Equipment or suspension systems to absorb vibrations, silencers, noise measurements.

Capital expenditure on pollution treatment includes expenditure on equipment for treating or measuring emissions and waste from production processes. Pollution treatment equipment deals with the by-products of production processes after they have been created. 

Examples include: 
- Equipment in wastewater treatment plants; 
- Air filters or scrubbers;
- Anti-noise barriers. 

Capital expenditure on pollution treatment also includes expenditure on land remediation, after mining or landfill.

Protection of biodiversity and landscape include:
- Land purchases for nature conservation purposes; 
- Reforestation schemes for conservation of species; 
- Rehabilitation of landscapes following quarrying of rock, sand and other minerals; 
- Planting of tree and shrub corridors around the perimeter of factories or business premises.

Minimisation of the intake of forest resources include:
- Paper recycling equipment;
- Wood recycling equipment;
- Recycled paper or wood products.

Production of energy from renewable sources include:
- Small, mini- and micro-hydroelectric facilities;
- Solar energy systems or equipment;
- Wind energy systems or equipment;
- Biomass energy (e.g. energy crops);
- Geothermal systems; 
- Wave and tidal systems; 
- Installation of renewable energy generation equipment.

Waste management include:
- Equipment for storage or transport of waste, e.g. vehicles/containers used strictly for carrying/storing waste; 
- Treatment or disposal equipment, e.g. recycling equipment, waste compressors, waste incinerators; 
- Equipment for sorting and separating waste; 
- In-house labour costs of sorting and separating waste; 
- Waste collection services provided by external companies.

Heat/energy saving and management include:
- Thermal insulation;
- Combined Heat and Power (CHP);
- Heat pumps.

Protection of ambient air and climate include:
- Purchase of new electric or hybrid vehicles; 
- Emission/odour/concentration monitors; 
- Equipment and installations for treating gaseous emissions, e.g. filters, scrubbers, centrifuges, purifiers, condensers; 
- Equipment to improve the dispersion of air pollutants into ambient air, e.g. higher stacks; 
- In-house labour costs of monitoring air pollution

